{
  "manufacturer": "Gree",
  "manufacturer_slug": "gree",
  "model": "Modbus Gateway (Mini) ME30-24/E6(M) for GMV multi VRF systems",
  "model_slug": "modbus-gateway-mini-me30-24-e6m",
  "short_model": "Gree ME30-24/E6(M)",
  "aliases": [
    "ME30-24/E6(M)",
    "Modbus Gateway(Mini)",
    "GMV5 Modbus gateway"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "VRF / split AC gateway",
  "applies_to": "Gree Modbus Gateway (Mini) on CAN-bus multi VRF systems (GMV5, GMV5 C/E/HR/MAX/MINI/SLIM, GMV Water, energy-recovery ventilation); Communication Protocol V2.0, multi VRF part only.",
  "summary": "The Gree Modbus Gateway (Mini) sits on the CAN bus of a GMV multi VRF system and serves up to 16 outdoor systems and 128 indoor units to a BMS over Modbus RTU. Holding registers carry per-indoor-unit on/off, mode, setpoint, fan speed and temperatures plus per-system outdoor data; coils carry feature flags, shields, locks and fault bits. Every indoor unit and system has an identical block, so this map lists indoor unit 1 and system 1 and gives the address rule for the rest.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "The protocol numbers words from 0 and coils (bits) from 0, and its example frames send the printed number unchanged (read word 1 sends 00 01, read coil 5 sends 00 05). Word n and Bit n are wire address n. Indoor unit n uses words from 102+25*(n-1) and coils from 288+64*(n-1); system m uses words from 3302+10*(m-1) and coils from 8488+48*(m-1)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Modbus Gateway(Mini) Communication Protocol V2.0",
    "doc_number": "V2.0",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.asami.lt/uploads/Products/product_78/me30-24_e6-m-_mini_modbus_variable_list_en_1708354351.pdf",
    "pages": "p. 8 serial settings, pp. 8-12 frames and addressing, pp. 13-17 BMS precautions, pp. 17-27 words (multi VRF), pp. 27-42 bits (multi VRF), pp. 85-91 DIP switches",
    "unofficial": true
  },
  "notes": [
    "Gree does not host this protocol publicly; the link is a copy on a Lithuanian distributor's site (Asami) and appears to be the unaltered Gree document.",
    "Only indoor unit 1 and outdoor system 1 are listed. The source prints identical blocks for indoor units 2-128 (words +25 per unit, coils +64 per unit), systems 2-16 (words +10, coils +48) and the 'subway' on/off blocks (coils +8 per unit or system).",
    "Left out: indoor ambient temperature (word 116) and outdoor ambient temperature (word 3307). Both are sent as x10 with negative ranges, but word 116 is typed 'floating-point' and word 3307 has no data type at all, so the 16-bit encoding is not settled.",
    "Words the source skips with '...' (for example 109-114 and 120-122) are not printed there and are not listed.",
    "Mode and fan words use one set of codes for writing and another for reading; the values list shows both.",
    "The fresh air unit sections (words 4200-13159, bits 11200-27583) are not included in this map.",
    "The protocol lists function codes 0x01, 0x03, 0x0F and 0x10 only; single writes (0x05/0x06) are not listed.",
    "The ME30-24/E6(M) part number comes from the distributor's product listing; the protocol document itself only calls the device 'Modbus Gateway(Mini)'."
  ],
